course: dictionary
lesson: 12147
title: Compartment: a separate part inside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A compartment is a separate part or section inside something bigger. It is a noun, so you can count it: one compartment, two compartments. «Put your pencils in the front compartment of your pencil case.» The pencil case is the container, and the front part is one section of it.
explain: Compartments keep things apart. «The freezer has a special compartment for ice cubes.» The ice cube part is separate from the rest of the freezer. Ask yourself: is this one part with a wall, lid or door around it? If yes, it is probably a compartment.
explain: Trains have compartments too. On older trains in the UK and Europe, each compartment was a small room with its own seats and its own door. «We sat in an empty compartment on the old train and played cards all the way to the sea.»
fact: Compartment means a separate part or section inside something bigger.
fact: A compartment can be inside a container, a bag, a car, a box or a railway carriage.
fact: A «glove compartment» is a small box in the front of a car where you can keep things.
fact: An «overhead compartment» is the space above your seat on a plane or train where bags are kept.
fact: Ships have compartments so that if one part springs a leak, the water stays in that part.
exercise: «Put your pencils in the front compartment of your pencil case.» What is a compartment here? | The name of the school | A pencil sharpener | *A separate section inside the pencil case | A loud noise
exercise: Which one is a compartment? | *The little box in a car's dashboard where you keep the maps | A big sandy beach | A green apple | A cloud in the sky
exercise: «The freezer has a special compartment for ice cubes.» Find and copy the word that names the separate part. | freezer | *compartment | special | ice
test: «We sat in an empty compartment on the old train and played cards all the way to the sea.» What is a compartment on a train? | The engine at the front | *A separate room with its own seats and a door | A long, thin carpet
test: «The ship's compartments kept the water out when one part sprang a leak.» Why are compartments useful on a ship? | They stop the sailors from getting hungry | They make the ship go faster in the wind | *They keep water in one part from spreading to the others | They are where the ship's flag is kept
exam: Which of these is a compartment you might find in a car? | *Glove compartment | A puddle | A cloud | A balloon
